  "notes": {
    "s1": {
      "fill": "teal",
      "maxH": 520,
      "text": "Version 2, in the Cyberpunk design system, following the Oct 13 user journey.\n\nWhat changed in the flow:\n• Catalogue items are strategy templates; the user runs their own strategy.\n• New template names: Dip in winners, The comeback, The big market drop, Your AI's top picks (Ride the long trend kept).\n• New step: choose the mode, Simulation or Live.\n• Budget and confirm are drawn in their Live variant; Simulation only changes the intro lines and the button.\n• Confirm adds the strategy name.\n• Discount zone, Choose stocks to watch, and the one-line disclaimer everywhere.",
      "w": 360,
      "x": -440,
      "y": 300
    },
    "s2": {
      "fill": "teal",
      "maxH": 420,
      "text": "Same layout as Dip in winners; the content differs per template.\n\n• Market drop and Long trend use one fund, which the user can change.\n• Ride the long trend lists a Buy rule and a Sell rule.\n• Your AI's top picks has no backtest. It shows what the AI reads, the prompt (read-only, with Edit prompt) and what the user needs.",
      "w": 360,
      "x": -440,
      "y": 2140
    },
    "s3": {
      "fill": "teal",
      "maxH": 520,
      "text": "Screens the first version didn't have.\n\n• Dashboard: Waiting for you on top; mode label on every card; a dot marks cards with something waiting.\n• Strategy page: Edit list for the stocks; removing one stops its signals, trades stay in the results.\n• Strategy page (live): You vs the rules on their own vs the index; per stock, what the rules hold vs what you hold.\n• Confirm a signal: I did it (price prefilled with the next day's open) or I skipped it (optional reason).\n• AI round: copy prompt, paste answer, pick the AI model, check scores, the sharing opt-in (off by default).",
      "w": 360,
      "x": -440,
      "y": 4020
    },
